{{also|farse}}
==German==

===Etymology===
From {{der|de|gmw-pro|*farsijā}}, derived (with {{w|Verner's law|Verner}} alternation) from {{der|de|gem-pro|*farzaz|t=bull, ox}}, whence obsolete {{cog|de|Farre}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|vaars}}.

The word is not attested in [[High German]] before the 15th century and apparently alien to modern dialects outside the borderlands with Low German. Therefore likely borrowed through {{der|de|gml|-}} and/or {{der|de|dum|verse}} (13th c.). The older High German word for “heifer” was {{m|de|Kalbe}}.
